 "audio_url": null,
 "note_en": "反而 (fǎn'ér) means \"instead\" or \"on the contrary\": the result is the opposite of what you'd expect. In this text: 他反而输了比赛 \"he lost the contest instead,\" and 做了多余的事，反而把事情弄糟 \"doing something unnecessary ends up making things worse.\" English often needs \"actually\" or \"ended up\" to get the same twist.",
